{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-17T08:43:52.133Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"ddb2e572b3dc24915ab9fe76","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-hw00c2","claim:pm-x07qz2","lineage:pm-x07qz2","lineage:pm-qwoy","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-hw00c2+pm-x07qz2","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-hw00c2","claim:pm-x07qz2","lineage:pm-x07qz2","lineage:pm-qwoy","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.326","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-bn3ppf"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"A key-named assignment inside a rejected reference value is never judged: the whole-value password grammar consumes a spaced command substitution, so the flat scan skips a password assignment written inside it"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Found 2026-11-17 while fixing pm-hw00c2. Since the whole-value password grammar (pm-ycgb5g, merged after the 2026.11.17 cut, so not yet released), password_assignment captures a value that is a spaced command substitution whole; it spells nothing, the match is rejected, and the flat scan resumes after the match, so a password assignment written inside that command (an echo of another password key with a literal value) is never visited. The published 2026.11.17 package reports that shape (measured against the npm tarball with scanMutationSecrets), and main does not, so this is a detection regression that would ship in the next cut. The structured pass is unaffected because it judges every key on its own. Fix direction: after a rejected flat match whose value holds a reference, judge each later key inside that value once, without rescanning inside those inner matches, so each character is scanned at most twice. Duplicate check: searched password command substitution inner assignment rejected value rescan; pm-ycgb5g (closed, introduced the grammar) and pm-jcz7qz (adversarial residuals) are related, and neither owns judging keys inside a rejected value."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:sdk","credential-redaction","regression","secret-guard","security"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-17T08:43:52.133Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-17T08:43:52.133Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":60},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A key-named assignment written inside a rejected reference value is judged at its own key in the flat scan, for every key-named rule; The rescan runs only for a rejected match whose value holds a reference and never recurses, so the linear-time controls still pass; The published 2026.11.17 verdict for a password assignment inside a spaced command substitution is restored"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-qwoy"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A password assignment inside a spaced command substitution is reported, as in 2026.11.17"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"main skips every key inside a rejected whole-value reference"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"secret-guard"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-hw00c2","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-17T08:43:52.133Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-ycgb5g","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-17T08:43:52.133Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"80687474b86765a503f982cd9a9135028e5c3efed4d96a9a4d7703f38841b1a4","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"9c0b07d2d85e2463305394c73b24b0cadef02f12202b80111588bb00d35e2fa6"}
